# What a command-line deploy uploads, held to the files the build actually needs.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS, measured rather than assumed. The working directory is 580 MB, and
# almost all of it is dependencies that the build installs for itself: 313 MB of Python
# virtualenv and 176 MB of node modules. A deploy run without this file was still
# uploading after five minutes and had produced no deployment at all, which is the least
# useful way for it to fail. Nothing appeared in the deployment list to say a deploy had
# even been attempted, so the symptom was a site that silently stayed on old code.
#
# The rule this file follows is parity with `.gitignore`: everything below is already
# excluded from version control, so nothing here is a new judgement about what matters.
# That keeps the list from drifting into a second opinion about the project's contents
# that has to be maintained on its own.
#
# Nothing excluded here is needed to build. `vercel.json` builds the front end with
# `npm run build` into `dist`, and the function's dependencies are installed from
# `requirements.txt`.

# Dependencies and build output. All of it is regenerated by the build.
.venv/
node_modules/
dist/
.build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
public/maplibre/

# Local state describing this machine rather than the application.
.vercel/
.git/

# Secrets. These hold real credentials, the build has no use for them, and an uploaded
# copy is a copy in a place nobody is auditing.
.env*

# Test artefacts.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/
.DS_Store
